time or entry is guaranteed.","source":"/en/plan/visa/"},{"topic":"keta-entry","q":"Age exemptions","a":"K-ETA-eligible travelers aged 17 and under or 65 and over are exempt from mandatory K-ETA. This does not itself exempt them from the e-Arrival Card.","source":"/en/plan/visa/"},{"topic":"keta-entry","q":"Fee and validity","a":"K-ETA costs KRW 10,000 plus the online payment fee and is non-refundable. Current approvals are valid for 3 years or until passport expiry, whichever comes first; this is not the allowed length of each stay.","source":"/en/plan/visa/"},{"topic":"visa:australia","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Australia","a":"No tourist visa needed — Australia passports are visa-free. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/australia/"},{"topic":"visa:australia","q":"Do travelers from Australia need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism Australia passport holders enter Korea visa-free. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/australia/"},{"topic":"visa:australia","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/australia/"},{"topic":"visa:australia","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/australia/"},{"topic":"visa:australia","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/australia/"},{"topic":"visa:australia","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/australia/"},{"topic":"visa:australia","q":"When does K-ETA come back?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/australia/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","a":"Yes — Bangladeshi passport holders need a visa. You'll apply for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa (single entry, stay up to 90 days). Fill the e-Form on visa.go.kr, print the barcoded form, and submit it in person at the Korean Embassy in Dhaka. K-ETA/visa-free entry does NOT apply to Bangladeshi passports.","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","q":"Do Bangladeshi citizens need a visa for Korea?","a":"Yes — for tourism you apply in advance for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa. Bangladeshi passports are not visa-free and not on the K-ETA list.","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","q":"Where do I apply?","a":"You fill the e-Form on the Korea Visa Portal (visa.go.kr) and submit the printed, barcoded form in person at the Korean Embassy in Dhaka (4 Madani Avenue, Baridhara).","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","q":"What is the e-Form?","a":"Since 2026 every applicant must complete the online e-Form on visa.go.kr and print it — the printout has a barcode that the embassy scans. Handwritten old forms are not accepted.","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","q":"How long does it take?","a":"Usually about 10–15 working days, and longer during peak season or if you're called for an interview or extra documents. Apply well ahead of your trip.","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","q":"How much does it cost?","a":"About US$40 for a single-entry short-term visa; roughly US$70 for double entry and US$90 for multiple entry. Amounts change — confirm the current fee at the embassy.","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","q":"What is a Bank Solvency Certificate?","a":"A letter from your bank confirming you are financially solvent. Bangladesh applicants are usually expected to submit it in addition to the 6-month bank statement.","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","q":"Can I get a multiple-entry visa?","a":"Double- and multiple-entry visas are available for a higher fee, but eligibility varies. Ask at the embassy about current rules for Bangladesh.","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:bangladesh","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card after I get the visa?","a":"The e-Arrival Card requirement can still apply on entry. Check the entry-document rules close to your travel date on the official sites.","source":"/en/visa/bangladesh/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Canada","a":"No tourist visa needed — Canada passports are visa-free. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"Do travelers from Canada need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism Canada passport holders enter Korea visa-free. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 180 days (6 months), for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"When does K-ETA come back?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"Do I need a return or onward ticket to enter Korea?","a":"Immigration can ask for proof of onward or return travel and where you'll be staying. Keep your ticket and accommodation details handy, even on a visa-free entry.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"How long can Canadians stay in Korea without a visa?","a":"Canadian passport holders get a longer visa-free stay than most nationalities — up to six months — though immigration still sets the length granted on arrival. Confirm the current terms before planning a long trip.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:canada","q":"What happens at the airport when I arrive?","a":"Complete the free e-Arrival Card shortly before landing, then clear immigration and customs. Have your accommodation address and return ticket ready in case you're asked.","source":"/en/visa/canada/"},{"topic":"visa:china","a":"Yes — Chinese passport holders need a visa for mainland Korea. Individual tourists apply for the C-3 tourist visa at a Korean consulate or Korea Visa Application Center. Two big exceptions can let you skip it: Jeju Island, and (at times) approved group tours.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"Do Chinese citizens need a visa for Korea?","a":"For mainland Korea, yes — individual tourists apply for a C-3 tourist visa. Jeju Island allows visa-free entry up to 30 days, and approved group tours have had time-limited visa-free windows.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"How does Jeju visa-free work?","a":"You can enter Jeju without a visa for up to 30 days, but only on direct flights to and from Jeju — you cannot transit through mainland Korea.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"Can tour groups still enter visa-free?","a":"A trial for approved groups of 3+ ran Sep 2025–Jun 2026. Because such schemes are time-limited, confirm the current status with your travel agency or the embassy.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"Where do I apply?","a":"At the Korea Visa Application Center or Korean consulate for the district where your hukou is registered.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"How much money do I need to show?","a":"No fixed minimum — show a stable 3–6 month balance plus ties to China. Fees are non-refundable.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"Entry-document rules such as the e-Arrival Card can still apply. Check the current rules near your travel date.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"How long does a Korea visa take to process?","a":"Once your documents are accepted, processing usually takes several business days, though it varies by season and by center. Apply well ahead of your trip and confirm the current turnaround where you apply.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"Do children need their own Korea visa?","a":"Yes — every traveler, including children, needs their own visa. A minor's application is submitted with a parent's supporting documents and proof of the family relationship.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:china","q":"What are the most common reasons a Korea visa is refused?","a":"Weak or unclear financial proof, an unconvincing trip purpose, incomplete paperwork, or applying at the wrong jurisdiction. Follow the document checklist and apply at the center for your registered address.","source":"/en/visa/china/"},{"topic":"visa:hongkong","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Hong Kong","a":"No tourist visa needed — Hong Kong (HKSAR) passports are visa-free. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/hongkong/"},{"topic":"visa:hongkong","q":"Do Hong Kong passport holders need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism, Hong Kong SAR passport holders enter Korea visa-free. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/hongkong/"},{"topic":"visa:hongkong","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/hongkong/"},{"topic":"visa:hongkong","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/hongkong/"},{"topic":"visa:hongkong","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/hongkong/"},{"topic":"visa:hongkong","q":"I hold a BN(O) passport — does this apply?","a":"This page covers the Hong Kong SAR passport. A BN(O) is a British passport and can follow different rules — check the requirements for that specific document before you travel.","source":"/en/visa/hongkong/"},{"topic":"visa:hongkong","q":"When does K-ETA come back?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/hongkong/"},{"topic":"visa:india","a":"Yes — Indian passport holders need a visa. You'll apply for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa (single entry, stay up to 90 days) in person at a Korea Visa Application Center. K-ETA/visa-free entry does NOT apply to Indian passports.","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:india","q":"Can Indians get a Korea visa on arrival or e-visa?","a":"Not for standard tourism — Indian passport holders apply in advance for the C-3-9 tourist visa at a Korea Visa Application Center. The Korea Visa Portal (visa.go.kr) is where you fill the form; some categories support e-application there.","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:india","q":"Do I need an appointment?","a":"No. In India you can walk in to the KVAC during working hours and submit; no prior appointment is required.","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:india","q":"How long does it take?","a":"Usually about 5–10 working days, but it can be longer during peak travel season or if extra checks are needed. Apply well ahead of your trip.","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:india","q":"How much does it cost?","a":"Roughly INR 3,400 for a single-entry short-term visa, plus the center's service fee (around INR 1,100–1,400). Amounts change — confirm the current fee at your KVAC.","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:india","q":"Which center do I go to?","a":"It depends on your state of residence. South Indian states go through the Chennai jurisdiction (Chennai, Bengaluru); the rest of India goes through the New Delhi/Embassy jurisdiction (New Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata and more).","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:india","q":"Can I get a multiple-entry visa?","a":"Multiple-entry tourist visas are possible in some cases (for example applicants with strong travel history), but eligibility varies. Ask at your KVAC or the consulate about current multiple-entry rules for India.","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:india","q":"What if I've never filed ITR?","a":"Submit a signed letter explaining why, and strengthen the file with a solid 6-month bank statement and, if relevant, a sponsor's documents.","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:india","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card after I get the visa?","a":"The e-Arrival Card requirement can still apply on entry. Check the entry-document rules close to your travel date on the official sites.","source":"/en/visa/india/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","a":"Individual Indonesian tourists need a visa — but groups may not. For solo/independent travel to mainland Korea you apply for the C-3 tourist visa. Since 28 May 2026, tour groups of 3+ can enter visa-free for short stays under a trial scheme — individuals are not yet eligible.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"Do Indonesians need a visa for Korea?","a":"Individual travelers need a C-3 tourist visa for mainland Korea. Since 28 May 2026, tour groups of 3+ can enter visa-free under a trial; Jeju Island has separate visa-free entry.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"I'm travelling alone — can I skip the visa?","a":"No. The visa-free trial applies only to groups of at least 3 people. Independent travelers must apply for the C-3 visa.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"What financial proof do I need?","a":"A 3-month bank statement plus an employment letter and salary slips. If sponsored, include the sponsor's documents.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"Where do I apply?","a":"At the Korean Embassy or the Korea Visa Application Center in Jakarta.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"How much is the fee?","a":"Fees vary and are non-refundable even if refused. Confirm the current amount at the center.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"Entry-document rules such as the e-Arrival Card can still apply on arrival. Check the current rules near your travel date.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"Can Indonesians visit Jeju without a visa?","a":"Jeju Island runs a separate visa-free entry program open to many nationalities, for a stay on the island only. Check the current eligibility list before you rely on it, as the rules change.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"How long does a Korea visa take to process?","a":"Once your documents are accepted, processing usually takes several business days, though it varies by season and by center. Apply well ahead of your trip and confirm the current turnaround where you apply.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:indonesia","q":"Do children need their own Korea visa?","a":"Yes — every traveler, including children, needs their own visa. A minor's application is submitted with a parent's supporting documents and proof of the family relationship.","source":"/en/visa/indonesia/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Japan","a":"No tourist visa needed — Japan passports are visa-free. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"Do travelers from Japan need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism Japan passport holders enter Korea visa-free. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"When does K-ETA come back?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"Do I need a return or onward ticket to enter Korea?","a":"Immigration can ask for proof of onward or return travel and where you'll be staying. Keep your ticket and accommodation details handy, even on a visa-free entry.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"Can I keep leaving and re-entering to stay longer?","a":"Back-to-back 'visa runs' to reset the visa-free period can invite extra questions, and immigration makes the final call at the border. Visa-free entry is for short visits, not living in Korea.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:japan","q":"What happens at the airport when I arrive?","a":"Complete the free e-Arrival Card shortly before landing, then clear immigration and customs. Have your accommodation address and return ticket ready in case you're asked.","source":"/en/visa/japan/"},{"topic":"visa:kazakhstan","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Kazakhstan","a":"No tourist visa needed — but you must apply for K-ETA. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/kazakhstan/"},{"topic":"visa:kazakhstan","q":"Do Kazakhstani passport holders need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism, Kazakhstani passport holders enter Korea visa-free and can stay up to 30 days. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/kazakhstan/"},{"topic":"visa:kazakhstan","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 30 days per visit, and no more than 60 days within any 180-day period. For a longer stay you'd need the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/kazakhstan/"},{"topic":"visa:kazakhstan","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"Yes. Kazakhstan is not on the temporary K-ETA waiver list, so you must apply for K-ETA before boarding — at the official site k-eta.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/kazakhstan/"},{"topic":"visa:kazakhstan","q":"How much is K-ETA and how long is it valid?","a":"It costs KRW 10,000 (about US$8), is valid for 3 years, and allows multiple entries. Apply only at k-eta.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/kazakhstan/"},{"topic":"visa:kazakhstan","q":"Do I also need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/kazakhstan/"},{"topic":"visa:kazakhstan","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/kazakhstan/"},{"topic":"visa:malaysia","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Malaysia","a":"No tourist visa needed — but you must apply for K-ETA. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/malaysia/"},{"topic":"visa:malaysia","q":"Do Malaysian passport holders need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism, Malaysian passport holders enter Korea visa-free and can stay up to 90 days. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/malaysia/"},{"topic":"visa:malaysia","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"Yes. Malaysia is not on the temporary K-ETA waiver list, so you must apply for K-ETA before boarding — at the official site k-eta.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/malaysia/"},{"topic":"visa:malaysia","q":"How much is K-ETA and how long is it valid?","a":"It costs KRW 10,000 (about US$8), is valid for 3 years, and allows multiple entries. Apply only at k-eta.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/malaysia/"},{"topic":"visa:malaysia","q":"Do I also need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/malaysia/"},{"topic":"visa:malaysia","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/malaysia/"},{"topic":"visa:malaysia","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/malaysia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","a":"Yes — Mongolian passport holders need a visa. You'll apply for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa (single entry, stay up to 90 days) in person at the Korea Visa Application Center in Ulaanbaatar. K-ETA/visa-free entry does NOT apply to Mongolian passports.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","q":"Do Mongolian citizens need a visa for Korea?","a":"Yes — for tourism you apply in advance for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa. Mongolian passports are not visa-free and not on the K-ETA list.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","q":"Where do I apply?","a":"At the Korea Visa Application Center (KVAC) in Ulaanbaatar (visaforkorea.mn), which handles applications for the Korean Embassy. You fill the form on the Korea Visa Portal, visa.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","q":"How long does it take?","a":"Usually about 5–15 business days, and longer during peak season or if extra checks are needed. Apply well ahead of your trip.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","q":"How much does it cost?","a":"Around US$40 for a single-entry short-term visa, plus the center's service fee. Amounts change and vary by visa type — confirm the current fee at visaforkorea.mn.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","q":"Does my bank statement need a Korean translation?","a":"No — the 6-month bank statement does not need to be translated into Korean, although some other documents may need translation. Check the current document list at the KVAC.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","q":"Can I hand in a handwritten form?","a":"No. Since 1 April 2026 the application form must be completed on a computer, printed and signed. Handwritten forms are not accepted.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","q":"Can I get a multiple-entry visa?","a":"Multiple-entry tourist visas are possible in some cases (for example with a strong travel history), but eligibility varies. Ask at the KVAC or the embassy about current rules.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:mongolia","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card after I get the visa?","a":"The e-Arrival Card requirement can still apply on entry. Check the entry-document rules close to your travel date on the official sites.","source":"/en/visa/mongolia/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","a":"Yes — Nepali passport holders need a visa. You'll apply for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa (single entry, stay up to 90 days) at the Korean Embassy in Kathmandu, by online appointment. K-ETA/visa-free entry does NOT apply to Nepali passports.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","q":"Do Nepali citizens need a visa for Korea?","a":"Yes — for tourism you apply in advance for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa. Nepali passports are not visa-free and not on the K-ETA list.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","q":"How do I get an appointment?","a":"Book online at koreanembassynepal.org. Slots open on Mondays and Wednesdays at 10:00 and fill fast, so book as early as you can.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","q":"How long does it take?","a":"About 21 working days, and longer during peak season or if extra checks are needed. Apply well ahead of your trip.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","q":"How much does it cost?","a":"NPR 5,400 for a single-entry short-term visa, paid in cash at the embassy counter. Amounts change — confirm the current fee at the embassy.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","q":"Do my documents need translation?","a":"Yes — Nepali documents must be translated into English and notarized. Any Korean documents must be originals issued within the last 3 months.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","q":"Why does the flight need to depart 21+ days after applying?","a":"The embassy expects your travel dates to allow for processing (about 21 working days). Book a reservation with a departure at least 21 days out — and never a fake ticket.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","q":"Can I get a multiple-entry visa?","a":"Multiple-entry tourist visas are possible in some cases, but eligibility varies. Ask at the embassy about current rules for Nepal.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:nepal","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card after I get the visa?","a":"The e-Arrival Card requirement can still apply on entry. Check the entry-document rules close to your travel date on the official sites.","source":"/en/visa/nepal/"},{"topic":"visa:pakistan","a":"Yes — Pakistani passport holders need a visa. You'll apply for the C-3 short-term tourist visa (stay up to 90 days) at the Korean Embassy in Islamabad. Some applicants are called for an interview, and tourist-visa extensions are generally not granted. K-ETA/visa-free entry does NOT apply.","source":"/en/visa/pakistan/"},{"topic":"visa:pakistan","q":"Do Pakistani citizens need a visa for Korea?","a":"Yes — for tourism you apply in advance for the C-3 short-term tourist visa. Pakistani passports are not visa-free and not on the K-ETA list.","source":"/en/visa/pakistan/"},{"topic":"visa:pakistan","q":"Where do I apply?","a":"In person at the Korean Embassy in Islamabad. You fill the form on the Korea Visa Portal, visa.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/pakistan/"},{"topic":"visa:pakistan","q":"Will I be interviewed?","a":"You may be. Some applicants are called for a short interview to verify their file, so keep your documents and answers consistent.","source":"/en/visa/pakistan/"},{"topic":"visa:pakistan","q":"How much does it cost and how long does it take?","a":"The fee and processing time aren't published in an accessible official source. Confirm both at the embassy before you book flights.","source":"/en/visa/pakistan/"},{"topic":"visa:pakistan","q":"Can I extend a tourist visa in Korea?","a":"Generally no — tourist-visa extensions are usually not granted. Plan your trip within the stay you're given.","source":"/en/visa/pakistan/"},{"topic":"visa:pakistan","q":"Can I get a multiple-entry visa?","a":"Multiple-entry tourist visas are possible in some cases, but eligibility varies. Ask at the embassy about current rules for Pakistan.","source":"/en/visa/pakistan/"},{"topic":"visa:pakistan","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card after I get the visa?","a":"The e-Arrival Card requirement can still apply on entry. Check the entry-document rules close to your travel date on the official sites.","source":"/en/visa/pakistan/"},{"topic":"visa:philippines","a":"Filipino passport holders need a C-3-9 tourist visa for mainland Korea. Submit through KVAC in the Philippines. Check the current KVAC instructions before visiting; the Embassy does not receive ordinary applications directly.","source":"/en/visa/philippines/"},{"topic":"visa:philippines","q":"Do Filipinos need a visa for Korea?","a":"Filipino passport holders need a C-3-9 tourist visa for mainland Korea.","source":"/en/visa/philippines/"},{"topic":"visa:philippines","q":"How much is the visa fee?","a":"For Filipino applicants: stays of 59 days or less have no visa issuance fee; stays of 60–90 days cost PHP 2,000. KVAC charges are separate; an agency may add a service fee.","source":"/en/visa/philippines/"},{"topic":"visa:philippines","q":"Do I need bank statements?","a":"The current tourist checklist lists a bank certificate, rather than a separate bank-statement item for ordinary employees. This is not a blanket exemption from financial evidence: follow your category and any additional request. Bank certificate: issued in your name within the last 3 months, showing account name, number, type, opening date, current balance and 6-month average daily balance (ADB).","source":"/en/visa/philippines/"},{"topic":"visa:philippines","q":"How long does it take?","a":"Effective 2026-10-01: ordinary C-3 processing is 12 working days; express applications remain 5 working days. Check express eligibility separately. Approval and entry are not guaranteed. Additional documents may be requested; the processing period may be recalculated after submission.","source":"/en/visa/philippines/"},{"topic":"visa:philippines","q":"Where do I apply?","a":"Submit through KVAC in the Philippines. Check the current KVAC instructions before visiting; the Embassy does not receive ordinary applications directly. If using an agency, choose from the Embassy’s current designated-agency list and confirm its submission arrangements.","source":"/en/visa/philippines/"},{"topic":"visa:singapore","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Singapore","a":"No tourist visa needed — Singapore passports are visa-free. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/singapore/"},{"topic":"visa:singapore","q":"Do Singapore passport holders need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism, Singapore passport holders enter Korea visa-free. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/singapore/"},{"topic":"visa:singapore","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/singapore/"},{"topic":"visa:singapore","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/singapore/"},{"topic":"visa:singapore","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/singapore/"},{"topic":"visa:singapore","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/singapore/"},{"topic":"visa:singapore","q":"When does K-ETA come back?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/singapore/"},{"topic":"visa:srilanka","a":"Yes — Sri Lankan passport holders need a visa. You'll apply for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa — a paper visa (single entry, stay up to 90 days) — at the Korean Embassy in Colombo. K-ETA/visa-free entry does NOT apply to Sri Lankan passports.","source":"/en/visa/srilanka/"},{"topic":"visa:srilanka","q":"Do Sri Lankan citizens need a visa for Korea?","a":"Yes — for tourism you apply in advance for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa, issued as a paper visa. Sri Lankan passports are not visa-free and not on the K-ETA list.","source":"/en/visa/srilanka/"},{"topic":"visa:srilanka","q":"Where do I apply?","a":"In person at the Korean Embassy in Colombo (No. 98 Dharmapala Mawatha, Colombo 7). You fill the form on the Korea Visa Portal, visa.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/srilanka/"},{"topic":"visa:srilanka","q":"How long does it take?","a":"A minimum of about 15 working days, and longer for some cases. There is no express service, so apply well ahead of your trip.","source":"/en/visa/srilanka/"},{"topic":"visa:srilanka","q":"How much does it cost?","a":"The fee is paid in Sri Lankan rupees at the rate in the embassy's current 'Visa Fee Increase' notice. Confirm the exact amount on the embassy site.","source":"/en/visa/srilanka/"},{"topic":"visa:srilanka","q":"Is there an express or urgent option?","a":"No. Early issuance is only available for diplomatic and official passport holders.","source":"/en/visa/srilanka/"},{"topic":"visa:srilanka","q":"Can I get a multiple-entry visa?","a":"Multiple-entry tourist visas are possible in some cases, but eligibility varies. Ask at the embassy about current rules for Sri Lanka.","source":"/en/visa/srilanka/"},{"topic":"visa:srilanka","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card after I get the visa?","a":"The e-Arrival Card requirement can still apply on entry. Check the entry-document rules close to your travel date on the official sites.","source":"/en/visa/srilanka/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Taiwan","a":"No tourist visa needed — Taiwan passports are visa-free. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"Do travelers from Taiwan need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism Taiwan passport holders enter Korea visa-free. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"When does K-ETA come back?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"Do I need a return or onward ticket to enter Korea?","a":"Immigration can ask for proof of onward or return travel and where you'll be staying. Keep your ticket and accommodation details handy, even on a visa-free entry.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"Can I keep leaving and re-entering to stay longer?","a":"Back-to-back 'visa runs' to reset the visa-free period can invite extra questions, and immigration makes the final call at the border. Visa-free entry is for short visits, not living in Korea.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:taiwan","q":"What happens at the airport when I arrive?","a":"Complete the free e-Arrival Card shortly before landing, then clear immigration and customs. Have your accommodation address and return ticket ready in case you're asked.","source":"/en/visa/taiwan/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"Korea Entry Guide from Thailand","a":"No tourist visa needed — but you must apply for K-ETA. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"Do Thai passport holders need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism, Thai passport holders enter Korea visa-free and can stay up to 90 days. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"Yes. Thailand is not on the temporary K-ETA waiver list, so you must apply for K-ETA before boarding — at the official site k-eta.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"How much is K-ETA and how long is it valid?","a":"It costs KRW 10,000 (about US$8), is valid for 3 years, and allows multiple entries. Apply only at k-eta.go.kr.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"Is K-ETA approval guaranteed?","a":"No. A K-ETA, and the final decision by immigration on arrival, are not guaranteed. Apply early, answer honestly, and carry genuine tourism documents — return ticket, hotel booking and proof of funds.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"Do I also need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism. Working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"Do I need a return or onward ticket to enter Korea?","a":"Immigration can ask for proof of onward or return travel and where you'll be staying. Keep your ticket and accommodation details handy, even on a visa-free entry.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"When should I apply for K-ETA before my trip?","a":"Apply on the official site k-eta.go.kr well before departure — the official guidance is to apply several days ahead — and leave buffer time in case anything needs fixing.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:thailand","q":"What happens at the airport when I arrive?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/thailand/"},{"topic":"visa:uk","q":"Korea Entry Guide from the United Kingdom","a":"No tourist visa needed — the United Kingdom passports are visa-free. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/uk/"},{"topic":"visa:uk","q":"Do travelers from the United Kingdom need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism the United Kingdom passport holders enter Korea visa-free. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/uk/"},{"topic":"visa:uk","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/uk/"},{"topic":"visa:uk","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/uk/"},{"topic":"visa:uk","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/uk/"},{"topic":"visa:uk","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/uk/"},{"topic":"visa:uk","q":"When does K-ETA come back?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/uk/"},{"topic":"visa:usa","q":"Korea Entry Guide from the United States","a":"No tourist visa needed — the United States passports are visa-free. The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/usa/"},{"topic":"visa:usa","q":"Do travelers from the United States need a visa for Korea?","a":"No — for short-term tourism the United States passport holders enter Korea visa-free. You do not apply for any tourist visa.","source":"/en/visa/usa/"},{"topic":"visa:usa","q":"Do I need K-ETA?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/usa/"},{"topic":"visa:usa","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"The e-Arrival Card is conditional. Valid K-ETA holders entering under K-ETA and valid Korean residence-card holders are exempt. A traveler entering with a visa may need the declaration even when also holding K-ETA. Other exceptions exist: use the official navigator for your documents and journey. This is an immigration declaration, separate from customs.","source":"/en/visa/usa/"},{"topic":"visa:usa","q":"How long can I stay?","a":"Up to 90 days, for tourism.","source":"/en/visa/usa/"},{"topic":"visa:usa","q":"Can I work or study on this entry?","a":"No. Visa-free entry is for tourism and short visits only; working or studying requires the appropriate visa.","source":"/en/visa/usa/"},{"topic":"visa:usa","q":"When does K-ETA come back?","a":"The temporary K-ETA waiver applies only to designated countries and regions through 2026-12-31. Visa-free entry does not automatically mean K-ETA exemption. Check the official notice again for later travel dates.","source":"/en/visa/usa/"},{"topic":"visa:uzbekistan","a":"Yes — Uzbekistani passport holders need a visa. You'll apply for the C-3 short-term tourist visa (stay up to 90 days). For tourism the Korean Embassy in Tashkent accepts documents ONLY through accredited travel agencies — you can't submit directly or online. K-ETA/visa-free entry does NOT apply.","source":"/en/visa/uzbekistan/"},{"topic":"visa:uzbekistan","q":"Do Uzbekistani citizens need a visa for Korea?","a":"Yes — for tourism you apply in advance for the C-3 short-term tourist visa. Uzbekistani passports are not visa-free and not on the K-ETA list.","source":"/en/visa/uzbekistan/"},{"topic":"visa:uzbekistan","q":"Can I apply directly at the embassy or online?","a":"Not for a tourist visa. The Korean Embassy in Tashkent accepts tourist applications only through travel agencies it has accredited. Employment, some student and government-program visas are submitted differently.","source":"/en/visa/uzbekistan/"},{"topic":"visa:uzbekistan","q":"Where do I find the accredited agencies?","a":"The official list is published on the Korean Embassy in Tashkent's website. Use only agencies on that list.","source":"/en/visa/uzbekistan/"},{"topic":"visa:uzbekistan","q":"How much does it cost and how long does it take?","a":"The fee and processing time aren't published in an accessible official source. Confirm both with an accredited agency or the embassy before you book flights.","source":"/en/visa/uzbekistan/"},{"topic":"visa:uzbekistan","q":"Where is the embassy?","a":"The Embassy of the Republic of Korea in Tashkent is at Afrosiyob Street 7, Mirabad District — but for tourism you submit through an accredited agency, not in person.","source":"/en/visa/uzbekistan/"},{"topic":"visa:uzbekistan","q":"Can I get a multiple-entry visa?","a":"Multiple-entry tourist visas are possible in some cases, but eligibility varies. Ask your accredited agency or the embassy about current rules.","source":"/en/visa/uzbekistan/"},{"topic":"visa:uzbekistan","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card after I get the visa?","a":"The e-Arrival Card requirement can still apply on entry. Check the entry-document rules close to your travel date on the official sites.","source":"/en/visa/uzbekistan/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","a":"Yes — Vietnamese passport holders need a visa. You'll apply for the C-3-9 short-term tourist visa in person at a Korea Visa Application Center (KVAC) in Hanoi or Ho Chi Minh City. The good news: the paperwork was simplified and long-validity visas are expanding.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"Do Vietnamese citizens need a visa for Korea?","a":"Yes, for mainland Korea you apply in advance for the C-3-9 tourist visa. (Ordinary passports are not visa-free for Korea.)","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"Can I get a 5- or 10-year visa?","a":"Korea has been expanding multi-year, multiple-entry visas for Vietnamese travelers. Eligibility depends on your profile and travel history — ask the KVAC/embassy whether you qualify.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"Where do I apply?","a":"At the Korea Visa Application Center in Hanoi or Ho Chi Minh City, depending on where you live, or the Korean embassy/consulate.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"How much money do I need to prove?","a":"There's no fixed minimum. Show a stable balance and strong ties to Vietnam. Financial proof is now simplified to 1–2 types.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"How much is the fee?","a":"Fees are set by reciprocity and vary; they are non-refundable even if refused. Confirm the current amount at your KVAC.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"I'm going on a company incentive trip — simpler?","a":"Yes. For company-organized group tours, the organizing company's guarantee can replace individual financial documents.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"Do I still need the e-Arrival Card?","a":"Entry-document rules like the e-Arrival Card can still apply on arrival. Check the current rules close to your travel date.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"Can Vietnamese travelers visit Jeju without a visa?","a":"Jeju Island runs a separate visa-free entry program open to many nationalities, for a stay on the island only. Check the current eligibility list before you rely on it, as the rules change.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"How long does a Korea visa take to process?","a":"Once your documents are accepted, processing usually takes several business days, though it varies by season and by center. Apply well ahead of your trip and confirm the current turnaround where you apply.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"},{"topic":"visa:vietnam","q":"Do children need their own Korea visa?","a":"Yes — every traveler, including children, needs their own visa. A minor's application is submitted with a parent's supporting documents and proof of the family relationship.","source":"/en/visa/vietnam/"}]}
